      "3.61::Supports BACnet/SC Certificate Exchange": "File 1, 3 and 4 take the clause 19.8.3 certificate writes (File_Size and AtomicWriteFile, applied by ReinitializeDevice); File 2 holds the CSR (PICS section 3).",
      "8.14::Supports receiving a DeviceCommunicationControl service request with an indefinite duration": "The DeviceCommunicationControl callback accepts a request with no Time_Duration; the stack runs the state machine.",
      "9.9::Supports B/SC over IPv4": "The hub function listens on wss://0.0.0.0:<sc-port>/ (IPv4); PICS section 7.",
      "9.9::Supports DM-TS-B": "TimeSynchronization is executed: SetSystemTime moves the clock behind Local_Date and Local_Time (PICS section 4).",
      "9.9::Supports DM-UTC-B": "UTCTimeSynchronization is executed: the clock behind Local_Date and Local_Time is UTC less the writable UTC_Offset (plus an hour while Daylight_Savings_Status is TRUE), both starting from the host's time zone (PICS section 4).",
      "9.9::Supports Non-hierarchical Network Port objects": "Both Network Ports have Reference_Port = none (4194303).",
      "9.9::Supports the DISCARD_CHANGES command": "Network Port Command DISCARD_CHANGES drops staged certificate writes (PICS section 3).",
      "9.9::Supports the GENERATE_CSR_FILE command": "Network Port 2 Command GENERATE_CSR_FILE makes a new key pair and CSR (File 2) (PICS section 3).",
      "9.9::Supports the Network Port Object Command property": "Command is writable on both Network Ports (cl. 12.56.16).",
      "9.9::Supports the Network Port object": "Network Port 2 (BACnet/SC), and Network Port 1 (BACnet/IP) when started with --port."
